  "question": "If $y = Ce^{-3x}$ is the general solution of a first-order differential equation, which of the following must be the correct differential equation?",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "Given $y = Ce^{-3x}$.<br /><br />Differentiate:<br />$\\frac{dy}{dx} = -3Ce^{-3x} = -3y$<br /><br />So,<br />$\\frac{dy}{dx} + 3y = 0$",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\frac{dy}{dx} + 3y = 0$",
    "B": "$\\frac{dy}{dx} - 3y = 0$",
    "C": "$\\frac{dy}{dx} + y = 0$",
    "D": "$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3y$"
